</ul>
<h2 class="astryx-heading level-2 primary x1tgivj0 x1xvnhcw x1cpk1wn x12yy4cs x1lliihq p1pc3f07 p13fuv20 p6gwkdc p11xkdxz phrwaqf pep27e5 p1adxfkp pmsqn1h" data-level="2" data-color="primary" id="muse-glimmer"><a to="#muse-glimmer" class="astryx-link primary x3nfvp2 x6s0dn4 x1lsbc85 xjb2p0i x1qlqyl8 x15bjb6t x1pd3egz x1hl2dhg x4ohgrr x1ypdohk x1mpt4pi xuedmi6 xlr8y92 x17nn4n9 x1wfwxd8 x7s97pk x1tgivj0 x4z56r7" data-color="primary" href="#muse-glimmer"><span class="astryx-text inherit primary x1tgivj0 x1qlqyl8 x15bjb6t x1pd3egz xt0psk2" data-type="inherit" data-color="primary">Build locally with Muse Glimmer</span></a></h2>
<p class="astryx-text body primary x1tgivj0 xjm74w1 xw6l6zx xxovm9e x1lliihq pfo4z36 p1ewvobj" data-type="body" data-color="primary">Muse Glimmer is an open-weight multimodal model, distilled from Muse Spark and built to run on your own hardware. You run it yourself instead of calling it over Model API: download the weights and serve them through a runtime such as vLLM, SGLang, llama.cpp, or ExecuTorch.</p>
<p class="astryx-text body primary x1tgivj0 xjm74w1 xw6l6zx xxovm9e x1lliihq pfo4z36 p1ewvobj" data-type="body" data-color="primary">Because Muse Glimmer is self-hosted, the API pricing and specs above don&#x27;t apply. Its own documentation section covers how to get the model, prompt it, deploy it, and customize it.</p>
